  "base_bias": {
    "status": "decided",
    "decision": "ship even-weighted (checks.md T15)",
    "column_meaning": "which Base school a zone's mobs flavour. This is permanent flavour: the owner ruled to SHIP EVEN-WEIGHTED, so no per-settlement frame weight is ever added and there is no keep-rate re-sim to wait for. The column may never carry a number a player can buy.",
    "checks": [
      "Ruled even-weighted: loot.md section 1 step 2 stays \"equal roll among all frames of that slot\" â€” no Base weight column is added, and the tools/loot.ts frame_weight path stays a what-if only.",
      "The three item-base.md paths (cloth 248 / balanced 390 / armored 657 weight) remain all reachable â€” even weighting means no settlement can make a school unobtainable, so the geographic-unlock worry never arises.",
      "No build must travel for a frame: frames roll equally everywhere, so Base bias is never a progression gate and world.md \"unlock by level\" is untouched."
    ],
    "forbidden_until_closed": [
      "numeric per-settlement Base weights (ruled out, not merely pending)",
      "any stock line that is the only source of a frame",
      "any gold price that buys frame odds"
    ],
    "closed_checks": [
      "Re-run the keep-rate simulation: tools/loot.ts measured it, and the Base-bias table inside the generated section 3 block shows the measured cost of a weight (armored x2.5 / cloth x0.4 moves the high-band keep-rate from 0.81% to 0.72%) â€” the owner chose NOT to pay that cost and to ship even.",
      "F3 drops/hour is unmoved by construction: a frame weight redistributes rolls inside one slot, and drops/hour comes from base_drop_chance x Lck, so no weight can change drop count."
    ]
  },
  "task_sizing": {
    "status": "provisional Â· owner-veto-able Â· ",
